      "jurisdiction": "North Dakota state courts",
      "method": "v1.1.0 case-law rebuild: authorities selected per decision point, each opinion retrieved from CourtListener and read; holding and quote taken from the opinion text; independently re-verified before release. Previous keyword-matched Justia listings were removed.",
      "verified_date": "2026-09-21",
      "key_cases": [
        {
          "case_name": "Suter v. Artist M.",
          "citation": "503 U.S. 347 (1992)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of the United States",
          "year": 1992,
          "date_decided": "1992-03-25",
          "holding": "The Court held that the Adoption Assistance and Child Welfare Act's requirement that a state plan provide for 'reasonable efforts' to prevent removal and reunify families creates no right enforceable by beneficiaries under § 1983 or directly, leaving enforcement to the federal agency's plan-approval process.",
          "relevance": "Explains why CFSR and plan-compliance review, not litigation, is the operative federal accountability mechanism.",
          "quote": "We hold that the Act does not create an enforceable right on behalf of respondents.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/112712/suter-v-artist-m/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 112712
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Interest of R.L.-P.",
          "citation": "2014 ND 28, 842 N.W.2d 889",
          "court": "North Dakota Supreme Court",
          "year": 2014,
          "date_decided": "2014-02-13",
          "holding": "The court affirmed termination of both parents' rights, holding the juvenile court did not clearly err in finding that social services made the reasonable efforts required by statute to reunify the family before termination.",
          "relevance": "Provides the state-court measure of the reasonable-efforts performance that federal CFSR review also tracks.",
          "quote": "This Court has recognized that juvenile court findings regarding whether the State made reasonable efforts to reunify children with parents is reviewed under the clearly erroneous standard.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/2653334/interest-of-rl-p/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 2653334
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Interest of A.L.E.",
          "citation": "2018 ND 257, 920 N.W.2d 461",
          "court": "North Dakota Supreme Court",
          "year": 2018,
          "date_decided": "2018-12-06",
          "holding": "The court affirmed termination, holding the juvenile court correctly applied the law and that clear and convincing evidence supported findings of deprivation, likely continuation of the causes of deprivation, resulting harm, and reasonable reunification efforts.",
          "relevance": "Supplies the state-court benchmark for the reasonable-efforts determinations federal reviewers audit.",
          "quote": "These elements must be established by clear and convincing evidence.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4348143/interest-of-ale/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 4570890
        },
        {
          "case_name": "In the Interest of A.B.",
          "citation": "2009 ND 116, 767 N.W.2d 817",
          "court": "North Dakota Supreme Court",
          "year": 2009,
          "date_decided": "2009-07-09",
          "holding": "The court affirmed termination, holding the juvenile court did not clearly err in finding by clear and convincing evidence that deprivation was likely to continue, that the child would suffer harm absent termination, and that the State made the reasonable efforts required by N.D.C.C. § 27-20-32.2 by offering an array of services the mother largely declined.",
          "relevance": "Enumerates the concrete service array (parent aide, case management, evaluations, counseling, nursing, parenting classes) that a state court treats as reasonable efforts, which is the same performance federal CFSR reviewers audit.",
          "quote": "The State is not required to \"exhaust every potential solution\" before seeking termination of parental rights.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/898561/in-the-interest-of-ab/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 898561
        }
      ],
